threads.body:
[General] `parameterSets` is resolved twice per request — once via `getValueForField` here and again inside `getListField` — and the field name literal is duplicated. A single lookup is enough and keeps the behavior identical: `ExecuteStatementRequest` has no `parameterSets` field, so the `Optional` is empty and this returns `null` (no `db.operation.batch.size`), while `BatchExecuteStatementRequest` always yields a `List` (an auto-construct empty list when unset), so the size is still reported, including `0`.

```suggestion
    Object parameterSets =
        sdkRequest(request).getValueForField("parameterSets", Object.class).orElse(null);
    if (parameterSets instanceof List) {
      return (long) ((List<?>) parameterSets).size();
    }
    return null;
```

